# Agent Instructions

`{{ .name }}` is an Intropy transactional integration: a .NET 10 job that
{{- if eq .source "sql" }}
reads the rows after its watermark from its source port's database once per
run, queues them as one message on an internal topic, and runs each queued
read through a send pipeline that writes to its destination port.
{{- else }}
sweeps its source port, queues each file on an internal topic, and runs each
queued file through a send pipeline that writes to its destination port.
{{- end }}

## Project overview

- App id: `{{ .appId }}`
- Internal topic: `internal-{{ .appId }}` on the system's pub/sub. It is
  invisible to the system topology; the framework reads both names from
  `INTROPY_PUBSUB_NAME` / `INTROPY_TOPIC_NAME`, which the system host and the
  deployment set.
{{- if eq .source "sql" }}
- Source port: `{{ .fromPort }}`, an external port (`PortRef.DefineExternal` in
  the system host's `Ports.cs`): a SQL query, no Dapr binding. Destination
  port: `{{ .toPort }}`, a Dapr binding declared in the same file.
- Query: `src/Sql/Query.sql`, embedded; the watermark column is `ChangeId`
  (`Delta.Column` in `Composition.cs`)
- Exit codes: `0` success, `1` a read could not be queued and its range stays
  pending, or a queued message was left for redelivery; `2` sidecar or
  internal queue unavailable
- Config keys (`src/appsettings*.json`):
  - `Ports:{{ .fromPort }}:Kind`: `Sql` (SQL Server); `Sqlite` in Development
  - `Ports:{{ .fromPort }}:ConnectionString`: a secret; Development reads
    `{{ .appId }}.db`, and the system host's development settings override it
  - `Ports:{{ .fromPort }}:InitialWatermark`: `int:0`, the watermark before the
    first run
  - `Ports:{{ .fromPort }}:CursorStore`: the state store the watermark is kept
    in, `{{ .cursorStore }}`; the system host and the deployment set it
  - `Ports:{{ .toPort }}:Kind`: `Local` in Development; a deployment sets
    `Ports__<port>__Kind` (`Sftp`, `AzureBlob`)
  - `PlatformServices:IdempotencyServiceAppId`: `{{ .idempotencyAppId }}`
  - `PlatformServices:BusinessIncidentServiceAppId`: `{{ .businessIncidentsAppId }}`
{{- else }}
- Source port: `{{ .fromPort }}`; destination port: `{{ .toPort }}`. Both are
  declared in the system host's `Ports.cs`.
- Config keys (`src/appsettings*.json`):
  - `Ports:{{ .fromPort }}:Kind`, `Ports:{{ .toPort }}:Kind`: `Local` in
    Development; a deployment sets `Ports__<port>__Kind` (`Sftp`, `AzureBlob`)
{{- end }}
{{- if eq .bodies "sample" }}
  - `PlatformServices:IdempotencyServiceAppId`: `{{ .idempotencyAppId }}`
  - `PlatformServices:BusinessIncidentServiceAppId`: `{{ .businessIncidentsAppId }}`
{{- end }}

## Important files

{{ if eq .source "sql" -}}
- `src/Configuration/Composition.cs`: DI registrations, the SQL source's query
  and delta (`ConfigureSource`), and `AddTransactionalIntegration`. The
  framework owns the receive side (read, publish, move the watermark); there is
  no receive-side component code.
- `src/Sql/Query.sql`: the source's query.
{{- else -}}
- `src/Configuration/Composition.cs`: DI registrations and
  `AddTransactionalIntegration`. The framework owns the receive side (sweep,
  publish, delete); there is no receive-side component code.
{{- end }}
- `src/Configuration/Constants.cs`: component name, ports, context keys.
- `src/Send/`: the send pipeline steps and `SendRoute`, which composes them.
- `src/Model/`: the `In`, `Out` and `Line` records.
- `test/{{ .name }}.Test.Unit/`: step unit tests.
{{- if eq .source "sql" }}
- `test/{{ .name }}.Test.Integration/`: receive-side watermark
  (`SqlReceiveTests`), send-pipeline and composition tests against a SQLite
  file and `Intropy.Framework.Testing` fakes (in `FakeEdges.cs`).
  `SqlReceiveTests` creates the table `Sql/Query.sql` reads; change them
  together.
{{- else }}
- `test/{{ .name }}.Test.Integration/`: receive-side, send-pipeline and
  composition tests on `Intropy.Framework.Testing` fakes (fakes in `FakeEdges.cs`).
{{- end }}
- `Dockerfile`, `Dockerfile.dockerignore`: image build. The build context is
  the system folder: `docker build -f {{ .appId }}/Dockerfile -t {{ .appId }} .`

## Build and test

{{ if eq .source "sql" -}}
The job runs via its system host, which provides the cursor store, the
destination binding, the pub/sub and the platform services.
{{- else -}}
The job runs via its system host, which provides the storage bindings, the
pub/sub and the platform services.
{{- end }}

```bash
task build
task test        # or task test:unit / task test:integration
task coverage    # Cobertura report under the integration project's TestResults/
```

## Development notes

{{ if eq .source "sql" -}}
- The pipeline works on bytes at both ends: the `Deserializer` receives one
  read's rows as a JSON array (one object per row, one property per column of
  `Sql/Query.sql`), and the `Serializer` returns the bytes the `Sender` writes
  as they are.
- The step bodies throw `NotImplementedException`; the send-pipeline tests
  are red until they are implemented. The model is an empty shell; give `In`
  the shape of the query's rows.
- Idempotency and business incidents key off the range each read covers
  (`WithSourceIdempotency` and `WithBusinessIncidents` in
  `src/Send/SendRoute.cs`): a range read again after a failed run is
  cancelled as a duplicate, and an incident is named by its range.
{{- else -}}
- The pipeline works on bytes at both ends: the `Deserializer` receives the
  source file's raw bytes, and the `Serializer` returns the bytes the `Sender`
  writes as they are.
{{- end }}
{{- if eq .source "sql" }}
{{- else if .empty }}
- The step bodies throw `NotImplementedException`. Idempotency and business
  incidents are not wired; add `.WithIdempotency(...)` and
  `.WithBusinessIncidents(...)` in `src/Send/SendRoute.cs` and register their
  clients in `src/Configuration/Composition.cs`.
{{- else }}
- Idempotency keys off the order's `OrderId` / `OrderDate`.
- The `Validator` fails with `Retriable: false`: bad data routes a business
  incident and the message is consumed. A destination write failure in the
  `Sender` stays retriable: the message is redelivered and nothing is
  committed meanwhile.
{{- end }}

